THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE THIS PROJECT INTEROPERATES WITH
================================================================================

This repository does not vendor, bundle, or redistribute any of the following.
It calls software the user installs separately, and reads file formats those
projects define.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LiteRT-LM  —  https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM
Copyright The ODML Authors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

    The inference runtime this plugin drives. The user installs it themselves
    (`uv tool install litert-lm`); this project starts its server and calls its
    OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

    `plugins/litertlm/tools/litertlm_backend.py` additionally imports modules from
    the user's own LiteRT-LM installation at run time (`litert_lm_cli.model`,
    `litert_lm_builder.litertlm_core`, `litert_lm_builder.litertlm_peek`) in
    order to read and rewrite the metadata header of a `.litertlm` file. No
    LiteRT-LM code is copied into this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FlatBuffers  —  https://github.com/google/flatbuffers
Copyright Google Inc.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

    Used indirectly, via the copy vendored inside the user's LiteRT-LM
    installation, to parse and rebuild the `.litertlm` metadata header.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LiteRT Community model conversions  —  https://huggingface.co/litert-community

    The `.litertlm` model files this plugin serves are published by the
    litert-community organisation on Hugging Face. Each model carries its own
    licence, which the user accepts when downloading it. This project neither
    redistributes nor modifies the weights.

    Note that repositories under `litert-community` are conversions and are
    distinct from the original vendor repositories (for example
    `google/gemma-4-*`), which have their own, sometimes stricter, licence
    terms. Gating differs per repository — verify rather than assume.

